<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Corn, wheat values steady.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Corn, wheat values steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf corn and winter wheat basis values were mostly unchanged, while nearby soybean values were higher and August lower, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Export markets were quiet. The U.S. Agriculture Department early Monday announced the sale of 240,000 tonnes of U.S. corn to an unknown destination. Grain dealers said the sale may have been to Spain, which dealers had talked about last week.</p>
<p>A lack of soybeans in market channels supported nearby CIF basis bids, dealers said.</p>
